  Statement of changes (Apache-2.0 §4(b)) — this file has been modified from
  the original:

    - Standardization parameters (per-feature means and standard deviations)
      learned during `fit` are stored on the model and re-applied at
      `transform` time, so new data lands in the same coordinate space as the
      training scores. The original standardized only at fit.
    - Fitting is seedable: the random initialisation of the loading matrix
      takes an explicit seed, making a fit reproducible run to run.
    - Model persistence round-trips the full parameter set (loadings, means,
      standard deviations, eigenvalues) rather than the loadings alone.

  The underlying method is unchanged: the EM algorithm for probabilistic PCA
  of Tipping, M. E. and Bishop, C. M. (1999), "Probabilistic Principal
  Component Analysis", Journal of the Royal Statistical Society, Series B,
  61(3), 611-622.
